<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Domestic sales moderate.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Domestic sales moderate.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal sales to domestic markets were moderate Wednesday, with most buyers seeking prompt shipment, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I had orders on Tuesday for shipment today,&quot; said a Midwest dealer.</p>
<p>Buyers continue to resist buying soymeal for July shipment because of the higher basis premium for that position.</p>
<p>Exports remained quiet with talk of small sales to Venezuela and Japan. One exporter said lower-priced Brazilian soymeal should keep U.S. soymeal exports light, until U.S. new-crop soymeal becomes available this fall.  </p>
